</head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#F6F5F1;">
<div style="display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0;color:#F6F5F1;">ines@arlet.test signed in with Google or GitHub on Thursday 15 October 2026 at 12:00 UTC; the old password was removed.</div>
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="background-color:#F6F5F1;">
<tr><td align="center" style="padding:40px 16px;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="max-width:560px;">
<tr><td style="padding:0 0 20px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.02em;color:#15151A;">Prismatica</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background-color:#FFFFFF;border:1px solid #DCDAD2;border-radius:6px;padding:32px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;color:#15151A;">
<h1 style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:24px;line-height:1.25;font-weight:600;color:#15151A;">Your sign-in was linked and your password removed</h1>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#15151A;">On Thursday 15 October 2026 at 12:00 UTC, someone signed in to the Prismatica account ines@arlet.test with Google or GitHub. The account already had a password, so to make sure only the owner of this mailbox holds it, we removed that password and signed out every other device.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 8px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;font-weight:600;color:#15151A;">What changed</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 16px 0;padding:0 0 0 20px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#15151A;">
<li style="margin:0 0 8px 0;">The old password no longer works. To use a password again, choose <strong>Forgot password</strong> in the sign-in window.</li>
<li style="margin:0 0 8px 0;">AI access tokens revoked: 2. Personal access tokens revoked: 1. Create new ones if you still need them.</li>
<li style="margin:0;">Members in workspaces you own, besides you: 3. Check that you know each of them.</li>
</ul>
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"><tr><td bgcolor="#B93A0C" style="border-radius:4px;background-color:#B93A0C;"><a href="https://prismatica.example" style="display:inline-block;padding:12px 20px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#FFFFFF;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px;">Open Prismatica</a></td></tr></table>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.5;color:#56565F;">This was not you? Open Prismatica, choose <strong>Forgot password</strong> in the sign-in window and set a new password at once, then review your workspace members.</p>
</td></tr>
<tr><td style="padding:20px 0 0 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#56565F;">This is a security notice about your account; it is sent whatever your e-mail preferences. Sent by <a href="https://prismatica.example" style="color:#56565F;">Prismatica</a> to ines@arlet.test.</td></tr>
</table>
</td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
"
`;

exports[`message accountLinked > matches its HTML and text snapshots > subject 1`] = `"Your sign-in was linked and your password removed"`;

exports[`message accountLinked > matches its HTML and text snapshots > text 1`] = `
"Your sign-in was linked and your password removed

On Thursday 15 October 2026 at 12:00 UTC, someone signed in to the Prismatica account ines@arlet.test with Google or GitHub. The account already had a password, so to make sure only the owner of this mailbox holds it, we removed that password and signed out every other device.

What changed:
- The old password no longer works. To use a password again, choose "Forgot password" in the sign-in window.
- AI access tokens revoked: 2. Personal access tokens revoked: 1. Create new ones if you still need them.
- Members in workspaces you own, besides you: 3. Check that you know each of them.

https://prismatica.example

This was not you? Choose "Forgot password" in the sign-in window and set a new password at once, then review your workspace members.

This is a security notice about your account; it is sent whatever your e-mail preferences.

Prismatica - https://prismatica.example
"
`;

exports[`message approveSignIn > matches its HTML and text snapshots > html 1`] = `
"<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
